{"id":"0822e827-2122-43ce-8191-2200458136d6","object":"chat.completion","created":1785028318,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"```json\n{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be dict\\\")\\n    nodes = case.get(\\\"nodes\\\")\\n    required_symbols = case.get(\\\"required_symbols\\\")\\n    if nodes is None or required_symbols is None:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"missing fields\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or not isinstance(required_symbols, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"invalid types\\\")\\n    node_map = {}\\n    children_map = {}\\n    depth_map = {}\\n    symbol_count = {}\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        nid = node.get(\\\"id\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(nid, str):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"id must be string\\\")\\n        parent = node.get(\\\"parent\\\")\\n        if parent is not None and not isinstance(parent, str):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"parent must be string or None\\\")\\n        symbol = node.get(\\\"symbol\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(symbol, str):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"symbol must be string\\\")\\n        depth = node.get(\\\"depth\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(depth, int):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"depth must be int\\\")\\n        removable = node.get(\\\"removable\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(removable, bool):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"removable must be bool\\\")\\n        node_map[nid] = node\\n        children_map.setdefault(nid, [])\\n        if parent is not None:\\n            children_map.setdefault(parent, []).append(nid)\\n        depth_map[nid] = depth\\n        symbol_count[symbol] = symbol_count.get(symbol, 0) + 1\\n    for sym in required_symbols:\\n        if sym not in symbol_count:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"required symbol {sym} not present\\\")\\n    root_ids = [nid for nid, node in node_map.items() if node.get(\\\"parent\\\") is None]\\n    if len(root_ids) != 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"must have exactly one root\\\")\\n    root_id = root_ids[0]\\n    retained = set(node_map.keys())\\n    removal_order = []\\n    changed = True\\n    while changed:\\n        changed = False\\n        candidates = []\\n        for nid in retained:\\n            node = node_map[nid]\\n            if nid == root_id:\\n                continue\\n            if node[\\\"symbol\\\"] in required_symbols:\\n                continue\\n            if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n                continue\\n            has_retained_child = False\\n            for child in children_map.get(nid, []):\\n                if child in retained:\\n                    has_retained_child = True\\n                    break\\n            if has_retained_child:\\n                continue\\n            new_count = symbol_count.copy()\\n            sym = node[\\\"symbol\\\"]\\n            new_count[sym] = new_count.get(sym, 0) - 1\\n            ok = True\\n            for req_sym in required_symbols:\\n                if new_count.get(req_sym, 0) <= 0:\\n                    ok = False\\n                    break\\n            if not ok:\\n                continue\\n            candidates.append(nid)\\n        if not candidates:\\n            break\\n        candidates.sort(key=lambda nid: (-depth_map[nid], nid))\\n        remove_id = candidates[0]\\n        removal_order.append(remove_id)\\n        retained.remove(remove_id)\\n        symbol_count[node_map[remove_id][\\\"symbol\\\"]] -= 1\\n        changed = True\\n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removal_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": retained_sorted\\n    }\"\n}\n```","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) according to the task description. This is SE-PE-01: grammar-guided node reduction. The case payload contains nodes (list of dicts with id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility) and required_symbols (list of symbols). We need to produce removed_node_ids (list of ids of nodes that are removed, in order of removal) and retained_node_ids (list of ids of nodes that are retained, sorted). The algorithm: deeper nodes first, then by id for tie-breaking. We cannot remove root, required symbols, or nodes with retained children (i.e., any child that is retained?). The description says: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" So if a node has any child that is retained, we cannot remove it. The process: iteratively consider tentative removals. For each node in order (depth descending, then id ascending), check if it's removable, not root, not required symbol (based on its symbol? Actually \"required_symbols\" are symbols, not node ids. So a node whose symbol is in required_symbols cannot be removed). Also check if all required symbols remain represented after removal (i.e., after removal, the set of symbols present in the tree (considering only retained nodes) must include all required_symbols). Also check that the node has no retained children (i.e., any child node that is retained). If all conditions hold, remove it (add to removed_node_ids), and continue. The process likely needs to iterate until no more removals possible. But the description says \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" Also \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes.\" So we need to do a pass over nodes sorted by depth descending, then id ascending. For each node, if it passes conditions, remove it. After removal, the tree changes (the node's parent might now have fewer children). But the condition \"node with retained children\" - if a child was already removed, it's not retained. So that condition is based on current retained child nodes. The algorithm might need to re-check after each removal because removing a node might enable removal of its parent? But order is deeper first, so parent is shallower and will be considered later. However, after removing a child, the parent might lose a retained child and thus become removable if it had only that child. But since we process deeper first, we will have already considered that parent? No, parent is shallower, so will be considered later (if we do a single pass after sorting all nodes). However, removing a node might also affect the \"required symbols remain represented\" condition for other nodes, but that condition is global. We need to decide if we process nodes in a single pass, re-sort after each removal, or iteratively until no changes. The typical Perses algorithm does iterative reduction: while there is a reduction candidate (node) that can be removed while preserving interestingness, remove it. The order is deterministic: deeper first, then by id. But after removal, the list of candidates might change (new candidates, some become invalid). The description: \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes.\" \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\" \"Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order.\" The actual removal order should be the order in which nodes are removed. So we need to simulate the process: repeatedly find the first node (by depth descending, id ascending) that is removable (check conditions) and remove it. Continue until no more removable nodes. That is standard. Implementation: start with set of retained node ids (all initially). Then loop: find candidates that are removable (based on current retained set). Sort candidates by depth descending, then id ascending. If any candidate, remove it (add to removed list, remove from retained set). Repeat. After loop, retained set is final. Then sort retained ids (by id? \"sorted retained IDs\" – presumably sorted by id, maybe lexicographically? Usually ID strings, sort naturally). The output: removed_node_ids in removal order, retained_node_ids sorted.\n\nBut we have to be careful: the condition \"node with retained children\" – a node has a retained child if any of its children (by parent field) is currently in retained set. So we need to build parent-child mapping. Also \"all required symbols remain represented\" – after removal, the set of symbols of retained nodes must include the required_symbols list. Note: root symbol is likely \"root\", and required_symbols includes \"root\" usually. So we cannot remove any node that would cause a required symbol to disappear. But required symbols are symbols, not node ids. Multiple nodes may have the same symbol. The condition is that after removal, for each required symbol, at least one retained node has that symbol. So we need to count occurrences per symbol. When a node is removed, decrement count. If any required symbol count becomes zero, that removal is invalid.\n\nInitial retained set includes all nodes. Then we iterate. Also \"Never remove the root\" – root is the node with parent null. So we skip that. Also \"Never remove a required symbol\" – that means any node whose symbol is in required_symbols cannot be removed? The description says \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" So if a node's symbol is a required symbol, it cannot be removed regardless of other conditions. So we must treat that as immutable.\n\nNow, implement solve(case) that returns {\"removed_node_ids\": [...], \"retained_node_ids\": [...]}.\n\nWe need to write Python code that uses only standard library, no external dependencies. Must raise ValueError for infeasible. When would it be infeasible? Possibly if a required symbol is not present in any node initially? But that's unlikely given inputs. Or if the root is not present? Possibly. We'll handle missing fields. According to \"Validate every required field before computing a result.\" So we should check that payload has nodes and required_symbols. Also each node has required fields: id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility. But we may not need utility. We'll check existence.\n\nNow, implement as described.\n\nSteps:\n\n1. Extract nodes list and required_symbols from case.\n2. Validate: nodes must be list, each must have id, parent, symbol, depth (int), removable (bool). required_symbols list of strings.\n3. Build maps: id->node, id->children list (initialize empty), also depth dict.\n4. Identify root: node with parent None.\n5. Initialize retained set = set of all ids.\n6. Initialize symbol counts: count per symbol from all nodes.\n7. Initialize removal order list.\n8. Loop:\n   a. Build list of candidate ids that are retained and not root. Also not required symbol (symbol in required_symbols). Also must be removable (node[\"removable\"] is True).\n   b. For each candidate, check if it has any retained children: for child in children[id], if child in retained, then skip.\n   c. Check if removal of this node would leave all required symbols represented: i.e., for each required symbol, count after removal (current count minus 1 if this node's symbol matches) >= 1. If any required symbol becomes zero, skip.\n   d. If passes, add to feasible list.\n   e. Sort feasible by depth descending, then id ascending (string compare).\n   f. If feasible empty, break.\n   g. Take first candidate, remove it: add to removal_order, remove from retained set, decrement symbol count for its symbol, and also update children? Actually parent-child relationship static; we don't need to update children list because condition \"has retained children\" uses current retained set. So next iteration children check will automatically consider that removed child is no longer retained.\n   h. Continue.\n9. After loop, retained_node_ids sorted (sort by id, string comparison).\n10. Return {\"removed_node_ids\": removal_order, \"retained_node_ids\": sorted(retained_ids)}.\n\nNote: The condition \"Never remove ... a node with retained children\" means if any child is retained, cannot remove. That is correct.\n\nWe must ensure we don't remove a node that has retained children even if those children are also removable? But algorithm will consider deeper nodes first, so children would be removed before parent if possible, allowing parent removal later. That's fine.\n\nNow, we need to produce implementation as a JSON string with key \"implementation\". The entire response must be a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source code as a string, properly escaped for JSON. We'll write the solve function.\n\nLet's draft code:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    # Validate\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"case must be dict\")\n    nodes = case.get(\"nodes\")\n    required_symbols = case.get(\"required_symbols\")\n    if nodes is None or required_symbols is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"missing fields\")\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or not isinstance(required_symbols, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"invalid types\")\n    # Build structures\n    node_map = {}\n    children_map = {}\n    depth_map = {}\n    symbol_count = {}\n    for node in nodes:\n        nid = node.get(\"id\")\n        if not isinstance(nid, str):\n            raise ValueError(\"id must be string\")\n        parent = node.get(\"parent\")\n        symbol = node.get(\"symbol\")\n        depth = node.get(\"depth\")\n        removable = node.get(\"removable\")\n        # also check utility present but not used\n        if parent is not None and not isinstance(parent, str):\n            raise ValueError(\"parent must be string or None\")\n        if not isinstance(symbol, str):\n            raise ValueError(\"symbol must be string\")\n        if not isinstance(depth, int):\n            raise ValueError(\"depth must be int\")\n        if not isinstance(removable, bool):\n            raise ValueError(\"removable must be bool\")\n        node_map[nid] = node\n        children_map.setdefault(nid, [])\n        if parent is not None:\n            children_map.setdefault(parent, []).append(nid)\n        depth_map[nid] = depth\n        symbol_count[symbol] = symbol_count.get(symbol, 0) + 1\n    # Check required symbols exist\n    for sym in required_symbols:\n        if sym not in symbol_count:\n            raise ValueError(f\"required symbol {sym} not present\")\n    # Identify root (parent None)\n    root_ids = [nid for nid, node in node_map.items() if node.get(\"parent\") is None]\n    if len(root_ids) != 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"must have exactly one root\")\n    root_id = root_ids[0]\n    # Initial retained set all ids\n    retained = set(node_map.keys())\n    # Implementation\n    removal_order = []\n    # Loop\n    changed = True\n    while changed:\n        changed = False\n        # Gather candidates\n        candidates = []\n        for nid in retained:\n            node = node_map[nid]\n            if nid == root_id:\n                continue\n            if node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols:\n                continue\n            if not node[\"removable\"]:\n                continue\n            # Check retained children\n            has_retained_child = False\n            for child in children_map.get(nid, []):\n                if child in retained:\n                    has_retained_child = True\n                    break\n            if has_retained_child:\n                continue\n            # Check required symbols after removal\n            new_count = symbol_count.copy()\n            sym = node[\"symbol\"]\n            new_count[sym] = new_count.get(sym, 0) - 1\n            ok = True\n            for req_sym in required_symbols:\n                if new_count.get(req_sym, 0) <= 0:\n                    ok = False\n                    break\n            if not ok:\n                continue\n            candidates.append(nid)\n        if not candidates:\n            break\n        # Sort by depth descending, then id ascending\n        candidates.sort(key=lambda nid: (-depth_map[nid], nid))\n        # Remove first\n        remove_id = candidates[0]\n        removal_order.append(remove_id)\n        retained.remove(remove_id)\n        symbol_count[node_map[remove_id][\"symbol\"]] -= 1\n        changed = True\n    # Sort retained ids\n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removal_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n\nPotential optimization: we are recomputing candidates each iteration, but that's fine. We copy symbol_count each time for check; could compute on the fly but fine.\n\nAlso we need to ensure that after removal, we don't need to update children_map because it's static. The condition \"has retained child\" is dynamic based on retained set.\n\nNow, we must output the code as a JSON string with proper escaping.\n\nLet's write the final response."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2172,"completion_tokens":3603,"total_tokens":5775,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2734},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":124},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}